title: qt layouts and size policies (pyside6)
url:   https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/overviews/qtwidgets-layout.html
tags:  qt pyside6 layout qvboxlayout qhboxlayout qgridlayout qformlayout stretch spacing margin size-policy resize align center spacer

; A layout places the widgets of one parent and resizes them with the window. Every container needs one.

## box layouts (QVBoxLayout / QHBoxLayout)
lay = QVBoxLayout(self)             # make a top-to-bottom layout and set it on SELF in one step  @vertical @column  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QVBoxLayout.html>
lay = QHBoxLayout()                 # make a left-to-right layout  @horizontal @row  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QHBoxLayout.html>
self.setLayout(lay)                 # set the layout on a widget (the widget takes ownership of children)  @set  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QWidget.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QWidget.setLayout>
lay.addWidget(W)                    # add a widget  @add  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.addWidget>
lay.addWidget(W, 1)                 # add a widget with stretch 1 (it takes the extra space; 2 takes twice as much)  @stretch @grow  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.addWidget>
lay.addWidget(W, 0, Qt.AlignmentFlag.AlignRight)  # add a widget aligned inside its cell (it no longer stretches)  @align  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.addWidget>
lay.addLayout(OTHER_LAYOUT)         # nest a layout (rows inside a column)  @nest @nested  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.addLayout>
lay.addStretch()                    # add flexible empty space (push widgets to one side)  @spacer @push  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.addStretch>
lay.addStretch(); lay.addWidget(OK); lay.addWidget(CANCEL)  # right-align buttons in a row  @right @buttons
lay.addStretch(); lay.addWidget(W); lay.addStretch()  # center a widget  @center
lay.addSpacing(20)                  # add fixed empty space in pixels  @gap @space  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.addSpacing>
lay.addSpacerItem(QSpacerItem(20, 40, QSizePolicy.Policy.Minimum, QSizePolicy.Policy.Expanding))  # add a spacer with its own size policy  @spacer  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.addSpacerItem>
lay.addStrut(N)                     # make the layout at least N px in the other direction  @min  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.addStrut>
lay.insertWidget(I, W) / lay.insertLayout(I, L) / lay.insertStretch(I)  # insert at a position  @insert  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.insertWidget>
lay.setStretch(I, N)                # change the stretch of item I  @stretch  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.setStretch>
lay.setStretchFactor(W, N)          # change the stretch of a widget  @stretch  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.setStretchFactor>
lay.setSpacing(N)                   # set the gap between items  @gap  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.setSpacing>
lay.setContentsMargins(0, 0, 0, 0)  # remove the border space around the layout (L, T, R, B)  @margin @padding  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.setContentsMargins>
lay.setAlignment(Qt.AlignmentFlag.AlignTop)  # stick all items to the top instead of spreading them  @align @top  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.setAlignment>
lay.setDirection(QBoxLayout.Direction.RightToLeft)  # reverse a box layout  @direction  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QBoxLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QBoxLayout.setDirection>

## QGridLayout
grid = QGridLayout(self)            # make a rows x columns layout  @grid @table  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html>
grid.addWidget(W, ROW, COL)         # put a widget in a cell  @cell  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.addWidget>
grid.addWidget(W, ROW, COL, ROWSPAN, COLSPAN)  # make a widget cover several cells (-1 = to the end)  @span @merge  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.addWidget>
grid.addWidget(W, ROW, COL, Qt.AlignmentFlag.AlignCenter)  # put a widget in a cell, aligned  @align  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.addWidget>
grid.addLayout(L, ROW, COL)         # put a layout in a cell  @nest  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.addLayout>
grid.setColumnStretch(COL, 1) / grid.setRowStretch(ROW, 1)  # let a column / row take extra space  @stretch  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.setColumnStretch>
grid.setColumnMinimumWidth(COL, PX) / grid.setRowMinimumHeight(ROW, PX)  # set a minimum column width / row height  @min  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.setColumnMinimumWidth>
grid.setHorizontalSpacing(N) / grid.setVerticalSpacing(N)  # set the gaps between columns / rows  @gap  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.setHorizontalSpacing>
grid.rowCount() / grid.columnCount()  # get the grid size  @count  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.rowCount>
grid.itemAtPosition(ROW, COL).widget()  # get the widget in a cell (itemAtPosition returns None if empty)  @get  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.itemAtPosition>
grid.getItemPosition(I)             # get (row, col, rowspan, colspan) of item I  @position  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.getItemPosition>
grid.setOriginCorner(Qt.Corner.BottomLeftCorner)  # count rows from the bottom  @corner  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QGridLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QGridLayout.setOriginCorner>

## QFormLayout (label: field rows)
form = QFormLayout(self)            # make a two-column "Label: field" layout  @form @label  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html>
form.addRow("Name:", QLineEdit())   # add a label + field row  @row  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.addRow>
form.addRow("&Email:", edit)        # & in the label gives Alt+E focus to the field (buddy is set for you)  @mnemonic
form.addRow(W)                      # add a widget across both columns  @span  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.addRow>
form.addRow(LABEL_WIDGET, FIELD_LAYOUT)  # use your own label widget or a layout as the field  @row
form.insertRow(I, "Label", W) / form.removeRow(I)  # insert / delete a row (removeRow deletes the widgets)  @edit  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.removeRow>
form.takeRow(I)                     # take a row out without deleting its widgets  @remove  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.takeRow>
form.setRowVisible(I, False)        # hide a whole row (label and field)  @hide  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.setRowVisible>
form.labelForField(W)               # get the label of a field  @label  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.labelForField>
form.setLabelAlignment(Qt.AlignmentFlag.AlignRight)  # right-align the labels  @align  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.setLabelAlignment>
form.setFieldGrowthPolicy(QFormLayout.FieldGrowthPolicy.AllNonFixedFieldsGrow)  # let fields grow to the full width  @grow  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.setFieldGrowthPolicy>
form.setRowWrapPolicy(QFormLayout.RowWrapPolicy.WrapAllRows)  # put each label above its field  @wrap @mobile  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.setRowWrapPolicy>
form.rowCount()                     # get the number of rows  @count  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QFormLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QFormLayout.rowCount>

## QStackedLayout
stack = QStackedLayout()            # show one child at a time (like QStackedWidget, as a layout)  @pages  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QStackedLayout.html>
stack.addWidget(W) / stack.setCurrentIndex(I)  # add a page / show one  @switch  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QStackedLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QStackedLayout.setCurrentIndex>
stack.setStackingMode(QStackedLayout.StackingMode.StackAll)  # show all children on top of each other (overlays)  @overlay  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QStackedLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QStackedLayout.setStackingMode>

## size policies (how a widget grows)
w.setSizePolicy(QSizePolicy.Policy.Expanding, QSizePolicy.Policy.Preferred)  # set horizontal and vertical policy  @grow @resize  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QWidget.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QWidget.setSizePolicy>
QSizePolicy.Policy.Fixed            # size is exactly sizeHint(); never grows or shrinks  @fixed  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.Policy>
QSizePolicy.Policy.Preferred        # sizeHint is best; may grow or shrink (default for most widgets)  @default  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.Policy>
QSizePolicy.Policy.Expanding        # wants as much space as possible; can shrink  @fill @grow  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.Policy>
QSizePolicy.Policy.Minimum          # sizeHint is the minimum; may grow  @min  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.Policy>
QSizePolicy.Policy.Maximum          # sizeHint is the maximum; may shrink  @max  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.Policy>
QSizePolicy.Policy.MinimumExpanding  # sizeHint is the minimum and it wants more space  @grow  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.Policy>
QSizePolicy.Policy.Ignored          # ignore sizeHint; take whatever space there is  @ignore  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.Policy>
sp = w.sizePolicy(); sp.setHorizontalStretch(2); w.setSizePolicy(sp)  # set a stretch factor through the policy  @stretch  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.setHorizontalStretch>
sp.setRetainSizeWhenHidden(True)    # keep the space of a hidden widget (no layout jump)  @hide @jump  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.setRetainSizeWhenHidden>
sp.setHeightForWidth(True)          # tell layouts the height depends on the width (wrapped text)  @wrap  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QSizePolicy.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QSizePolicy.setHeightForWidth>
lay.setSizeConstraint(QLayout.SizeConstraint.SetFixedSize)  # make the window always exactly as big as its content  @fixed @shrink  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.setSizeConstraint>
lay.setSizeConstraint(QLayout.SizeConstraint.SetMinimumSize)  # stop the window from getting smaller than its content  @min  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.setSizeConstraint>

## manage items
lay.count()                         # get the number of items  @count  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.count>
lay.itemAt(I).widget()              # get the widget of item I (None for spacers and layouts)  @get  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.itemAt>
lay.itemAt(I).layout()              # get the nested layout of item I  @nested  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayoutItem.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayoutItem.layout>
lay.indexOf(W)                      # get the index of a widget  @find  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.indexOf>
lay.removeWidget(W)                 # take a widget out of the layout (it stays on screen until deleted or reparented)  @remove  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.removeWidget>
lay.replaceWidget(OLD, NEW)         # put NEW where OLD was  @swap  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.replaceWidget>
lay.takeAt(I)                       # remove item I and return it  @remove  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.takeAt>
while lay.count(): item = lay.takeAt(0); w = item.widget(); w and w.deleteLater()  # remove and delete everything in a layout  @clear @empty
    def clear_layout(lay):
        while lay.count():
            item = lay.takeAt(0)
            if item.widget(): item.widget().deleteLater()
            elif item.layout(): clear_layout(item.layout())
lay.invalidate() / lay.activate()   # force the layout to recompute now  @refresh  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.activate>
lay.setEnabled(False)               # stop the layout from moving widgets  @freeze  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.setEnabled>
lay.parentWidget()                  # get the widget the layout manages  @parent  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.parentWidget>
lay.setMenuBar(MENUBAR)             # put a menu bar at the top of a plain widget  @menu  <https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/PySide6/QtWidgets/QLayout.html#PySide6.QtWidgets.QLayout.setMenuBar>

## tips
QWidget::setLayout: Attempting to set QLayout "" on X, which already has a layout  # a widget has one layout; nest more with addLayout  @error
widgets not showing                 # you created them without adding them to a layout or giving them a parent  @invisible @missing
window will not shrink              # a child has a large minimumSize or a Fixed/Minimum policy  @resize
QMainWindow                         # never call setLayout on it; give setCentralWidget a QWidget that has the layout  @mainwindow
hide() and show()                   # hidden widgets give up their space in the layout; setRetainSizeWhenHidden keeps it  @hide
Qt Designer                         # build layouts visually: select widgets, right click > Lay out  @designer
